# out/ holds generated figures. The SVGs are part of the published site --
# index.html and the decks load out/fig01-*.svg and Pages serves the repo as-is
# -- so they are tracked and CI checks them for drift. The PDFs are build
# products only.
out/*
!out/*.svg

# The three pages the site publishes are tracked, and so are the two decks'
# asset directories: Pages serves this repository as-is, so index.html,
# core-pitch.html, full-pitch.html and core-pitch_files/, full-pitch_files/ are
# the deployed site. Only index.html embeds its resources -- it is one page
# with one photograph, and self-containing it costs a megabyte. The decks do
# not: embedding reveal.js and the title photograph into each of them produced
# 5.4 MB files that would be rewritten in full on every render.
index_files/

# figures.html/pdf and slides.html are working documents rather than pages of
# the site: nothing on it links to them, and figures.html alone is over a
# megabyte. They are rebuilt by `quarto render` and uploaded as CI artifacts.
figures.html
figures.pdf
figures_files/
slides.html
slides_files/

# The gallery's source photographs. index.qmd embeds its resources, so what
# the page actually carries is images/gallery/ -- 1100 px derivatives built by
# tools/make-gallery.ps1 -- and those are tracked, which is what lets CI render
# index.html from a clean clone. The originals below are 6000 px camera and
# phone files of 29 MB between them, read by nothing but that script, and they
# are not worth putting in a repository GitHub Pages serves as-is. They are
# therefore NOT backed up here: keep them wherever the project's other raw
# photographs live. images/kamera_web.jpg and images/20250703024959-snapshot.jpg
# are already small enough to track, and the hero loads the latter directly.
images/ami_system_PSX_*.jpg
images/nahravace_PSX_*.jpg
images/Obr_2_CamAlien_*.JPG
images/abms_ai_interface.png

